            "review_title": "Review at Together Korea Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Kathy L\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam7 contributions\n0\nBad Food\nJun 2017 • Solo\nI`m not Korean, but I love Korean food. I`ve visited dozens of Korean restaurants before and cooked Korean food with my friends from Korea. This food is nothing like I`ve eaten before.\nJajang ramyun is cheap noodles with no meat,no sesame and no egg! Even though on the picture it has sesame,meat and sliced egg in half too! When I asked the waiter why the difference is so big, she just shook her head ans said \"no, its like this\".Its the same quality and quantity if you buy instant jajang for 30k in LotteMart. It`s not gross, but very very poor. Not fit for a restaurant.\n\nToppoki with cheese were OK. A little bit of cheese, a little bit of toppoki, portion is very small for 120k. in saigon I could eat 3 course meal in any korean restaurant for this money. Also, very little and not delicious. \nThe only thing I really liked- is kimchi. It tasted authentic and like the ones in Korea,\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten June 5, 2017",
